# SFT execution status v0.121: generated-only Linux launcher

2026-09-27. Implemented a systemd-backed **generated-only rehearsal launcher**
and worker entry. Local verification passes **120 tests**: 32 new dispatch,
resource-readback and attempt tests, plus the previous 88 CPU import/package
tests. Ruff passes. The Mac CLI rejects launch before any worker dispatch.

**No native Linux rehearsal has run. Gate 5 is not complete.** This is concrete
launcher code, not a claim that Mac mocks prove Linux containment. It connects
the existing real tiny import/package integration suite to a fixed supervised
worker. It does not yet connect real input acquisition or the full-size
coordinator; those old execution entrypoints remain unchanged and closed.

## Implemented path

`admitted dedicated VM -> pinned staged source -> exclusive attempt marker
-> four sequential systemd services -> aggregate result / fixed failure code`

The CLI has no model, dataset, checkpoint path, download, arbitrary command or
training argument. It binds a supplied machine ID and a pre-staged source
manifest. Before dispatch it requires Linux, root, systemd >= 255, cgroup v2,
the memory/pids/CPU controllers, and a fresh private attempt directory.
It never provisions a machine, installs software, contacts S3, or starts a GPU.

| Native case, once separately admitted | Worker RAM cap | Runtime cap | Required result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Real generated DCP/package/reload integration | 2 GiB | 120 s | All four existing integration cases pass |
| Timeout, including a child process | 128 MiB | 2 s | systemd timeout, then empty workload cgroup |
| Memory exhaustion | 96 MiB | 15 s | systemd reports OOM kill, then empty workload cgroup |
| Temporary-storage exhaustion | 256 MiB | 15 s | Near-full 64-MiB tmpfs followed by ENOSPC, then empty cgroup |

Each worker requests no swap, at most 64 tasks, one CPU's quota, UID/GID 10001,
no capabilities, private network/devices, read-only host filesystem and a fresh
64-MiB `/work` tmpfs. Worker stdout/stderr go to null; records retain only fixed
codes and aggregates. Model library output and exception text are not saved.
Worker entry checks cgroup identity, RAM/swap/task caps, temporary filesystem
size/ownership and offline environment before imports or probe allocation.

The launcher reserves the attempt before the first dispatch, executes each
case once, and stops the sequence on failure. It checks for an existing unit
before dispatch so it does not stop a pre-existing service. On an ambiguous
start or later failure it attempts exactly one stop of its own named service;
an unconfirmed stop or populated cgroup cannot produce a pass.

The controller's overall dispatch window is 240 seconds; bounded final cleanup
can extend beyond it. The per-worker systemd deadlines are independent of the
controller. Controller-death recovery and a host's billing lifecycle have not
been qualified by these local tests. The implementation does not stop or
terminate cloud instances and does not enforce their total bill.

## Important scope limits

- The 32 new tests double systemd/native boundaries. The retained CPU integration
  tests use genuine tiny tensors but no forward/optimizer step or real payloads.
- No native memory/disk exhaustion was deliberately run on the Mac. The four
  native probes must run only on a separately approved dedicated Linux VM.
- The source-manifest check is not an independent proof of publisher origin.
  The operator must authenticate the launcher before executing it and separately
  authenticate/stage its runtime. The source manifest does not cover venv wheels.
- A storage-capacity limit is not a cumulative-native-write limit. The old host
  contract is preserved, not silently satisfied or overwritten by this route.
- Failed real-import evidence is untouched. The rehearsal's own generated
  fixtures are ephemeral tmpfs content; only aggregate run records persist.
- Production eligibility, real-4B import verification and training authority
  remain false. No existing busy Lambda instance may be reused for this work.

## Next action and required staging

There is no admitted Linux target yet. The Mac has no `docker`, `colima`,
`limactl`, or QEMU executable on the checked PATH. Do not rent a GPU for this
rehearsal. Obtain a dedicated CPU-only Linux target and explicit duration/cost
and lifecycle limits before remote work or provisioning.

After target admission, prepare `/opt/lumi-sft-rehearsal` with the authenticated
runtime at `venv/bin/python`, the new script under `scripts/`, and the source
and test dependency closure under flat `src/lumi/` and `tests/` directories.
Create the dedicated UID/GID 10001 account with no unrelated supplementary
groups. Stage code as root-owned, non-writable by the worker, with no symlinks,
hardlinks, bytecode, data, or undeclared files in those source directories.
Stage `release-manifest.json` as a relative-source-name to SHA-256 JSON mapping
covering those exact directories. Independently pin its file hash. The runtime
must be compatible with the already tested torch/transformers stack; do not
silently substitute an unverified image. These staging actions were not run.

The operator-created `/var/lib/lumi-sft-rehearsal` must be root-owned mode 0700.
The launch CLI then requires `--expected-machine-id`, a fresh 32-hex `--attempt`,
and `--release-sha256`; none is filled with guessed host data. A failure retains
its marker and fixed-code failure record. There is no automatic retry.

After native generated-only acceptance, the remaining Gate-5 work is the
host-bound real-input/full-size-coordinator adapter and independently verified
real checkpoint import. Gate 6 still requires SFT-specific pre-dispatch approval,
GPU smoke/save/resume acceptance and the full SFT run. No such steps were skipped
or marked done here.

## Files and verification

- `src/lumi/posttraining_import_vm_rehearsal_v1.py`
- `scripts/run_sft_import_vm_rehearsal_v1.py`
- `tests/test_sft_import_vm_rehearsal_v1.py`
- `evidence/lumi-4b-sft-vm-rehearsal-development-v0.1.json`

Reproduce the new portable tests with the existing environment:

```sh
PYTHONPATH=src PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \
artifacts/lumi-sft-import-runtime-v0.1/venv/bin/python -B -m unittest \
  tests.test_sft_import_vm_rehearsal_v1
```

The final combined run used the same offline/CPU-only audit harness as v0.120,
adding this module. It passed 120/120 without skips or prohibited audit events.
The direct Mac CLI negative check returned `host_rejected_linux_required` with
exit code 2. No real model/tokenizer/dataset reads, GPU, inference, training,
remote machine actions, staging, commit or push occurred. Public systemd
documentation was consulted; this is not a whole-turn zero-network claim.

The implementation follows systemd's documented service lifetime and resource
controls, not equivalence with the old per-write broker contract:
[service controls](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/systemd/systemd/v255/man/systemd.service.xml),
[execution isolation and groups](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/systemd/systemd/v255/man/systemd.exec.xml),
[resource controls](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/systemd/systemd/v255/man/systemd.resource-control.xml).
